  "description": "Colorado's 1st Congressional District covers almost all of Denver, along with the enclaves of Glendale and Holly Hills. Incumbent Democrat Diana DeGette, first elected in 1996, faces a competitive Democratic primary challenge from University of Colorado Regent Wanda James and attorney Melat Kiros ahead of the June 30 primary. The district is rated Safe/Solid Democratic by major nonpartisan forecasters, but the primary contest reflects ideological divisions within the party on issues such as Israel-Palestine policy, Medicare for All, and incremental versus progressive change. The Republican nominee is presumptive candidate Christy Peterson, while Libertarian Chad Humphrey and Unity Party candidate Critter Milton are also on the general election ballot.",
